tests:
perch/tests/runs.rs. Seed a chat the way tests/term.rs:497-498 does: create <site.home>/sessions and write <id>.eid into it (site() does not make sessions/, tests/runs.rs:81-91).
- a_chat_that_is_not_a_chat_id_is_a_400_and_nothing_is_made, on site.quiet:
  - chat = 7, true, {}, "", "../x", "a/b", "a\nb", "%2e", ".x", and 129 bytes each give a 400 whose body has "error";
  - chat = 128 bytes of [a-z] is NOT refused for its shape: it gets the 404 of an unknown chat;
  - afterwards neither runs/ nor runs.json exists.
- a_chat_the_perch_does_not_know_is_a_404_with_a_sentence_and_nothing_is_made: a well-formed unknown id gives 404 with "error":"no such chat" (body not empty), and nothing is made. It comes before the holder and the health checks: on site.quiet(&["--run-graphs", "wiki-hop", "--jev-health", <a closed loopback port>]) an unknown chat still gets the 404, while a well-formed start with no chat gets the 503.
- a_run_started_beside_a_chat_keeps_the_chat_on_every_answer (FAKE_WORKFLOW_CASE=a), for a seeded chat c0ffee01:
  - the 202 is exactly {rid:"r1", state:"running", chat:"c0ffee01"};
  - after done, the detail and the list row have chat c0ffee01;
  - <home>/runs.json r1.chat is c0ffee01;
  - nothing under <home>/runs/r1/ (config.toml, args.json, out.log, err.log) contains c0ffee01: the chat never reached the child.
- a_run_with_no_chat_is_what_it_was_before: a start with no chat and one with chat:null give exactly {rid, state}; neither the row, the detail nor runs.json has a chat key.
- a_chat_the_perch_remembers_but_cannot_list_is_known: write <home>/chat-cwds.json naming c0ffee02 with an existing folder and no log (the tests/term.rs:494 pattern); a start with chat c0ffee02 gets 202.
- the_list_takes_one_chat_and_keeps_fifty_of_its_runs:
  - write runs.json BEFORE the perch starts: r1..r60 done with chat aa, r61..r120 done with chat bb, r121..r130 done with no chat;
  - ?chat=aa gives 50 rows, every one chat aa, r60 first and r11 last;
  - ?chat=bb gives r120..r71;
  - no query gives r130..r81;
  - ?chat=gone gives [].
- a_list_query_other_than_one_chat_is_a_400: ?chat=, ?chat=a&chat=b, ?x=1, ?limit=5, ?chat=a&x=1, ?chat=a%2Fb, ?chat=.., ?chat=a=b each give 400 with "error".
- a_chat_written_into_runs_json_by_hand_is_left_off_the_row: runs.json with r1.chat "../etc", r2.chat "a b", r3.chat "<b>x</b>", r4.chat of 200 bytes and r5.chat "ok1"; the list and each detail have no chat key for r1-r4 and chat "ok1" for r5.
- the_holder_409_names_its_chat (FAKE_WORKFLOW_CASE=b, which parks): seed c0ffee01 and c0ffee02, start beside c0ffee01, wait for parked. A second start with no chat, and one beside the other seeded chat c0ffee02, are each a 409 with run "r1" and chat "c0ffee01"; the sentence is unchanged. Not "any chat": an unknown chat is refused 404 before the holder check is reached.
- an_unknown_chat_is_a_404_even_while_a_run_holds_the_browser: with r1 still parked, a start naming a well-formed unknown chat gets the 404 "no such chat", not the 409. This pins the order: the existence check runs before the holder check (state.rs:530).
- cancel_and_abandon_answers_carry_the_chat: abandon of the parked run above answers a row with chat c0ffee01.
- Unit tests in state.rs:
  - chat_query over every case above;
  - row() leaves off a bad tag and keeps a good one;
  - begin(.., Some(chat)) stores it in the same write (read runs.json straight after begin);
  - the 9 existing begin(…, None) calls (state.rs:738-799) and Run::new("g", None) (state.rs:820) gain the new argument.
- Each new test must go red when its line of the change is reverted (check by hand once, and list the reverts in the report).
- Whole suite once (--features test-bins), clippy clean with --all-targets -D warnings.
- serve.rs pins need no change: the routing is unchanged (serve.rs:592-594, 632; the query pin at serve.rs:1256 routes only). If one goes red, name it and stop.
